### Steps to reproduce

1. Run the code sample below. It rebuilds once a second and, every 3 seconds, moves the `ReorderableListView` to a new parent through a `GlobalKey` (the app bar title flips between "wrapped" and "not wrapped").
2. Long-press item **B** so it lifts, and keep holding it until the title flips.
3. Release it **where it started**, so the order does not change.

### Expected results

The item drops back into place and keeps rendering normally.

### Actual results

The item turns into an error widget and throws on every later rebuild (here once a second, from the timer):

```
Null check operator used on a null value
#0      _ReorderableItemState.build (package:flutter/src/widgets/reorderable_list.dart:1294:57)
#1      StatefulElement.build (package:flutter/src/widgets/framework.dart:5944:27)
...
```

The drop itself usually also throws once:

```
Null check operator used on a null value
#0      SliverReorderableListState._itemOffsetAt (package:flutter/src/widgets/reorderable_list.dart:1132:25)
#1      SliverReorderableListState._dragEnd.<anonymous closure> (package:flutter/src/widgets/reorderable_list.dart:948:30)
```

We first saw it in production: release build 3.47.1 on iOS 26.6.2. A card in a reorderable list rendered as a grey box and threw once a second, because the page rebuilds every second, until the user left the screen.

### Cause

What I found by reading `reorderable_list.dart`:

- `_ReorderableItemState.deactivate()` calls `_listState._unregisterItem(index, this)`.
- Nothing re-registers the item on `activate()`. Registration only happens in `initState`, `didUpdateWidget` and `build`.
- `build` returns the drag placeholder **before** it calls `_registerItem`:
  ```dart
  if (_dragging) {
    final Size size = _extentSize(_listState._dragInfo!.itemExtent, _listState._scrollDirection);
    return SizedBox.fromSize(size: size);
  }
  _listState._registerItem(this);
  ```
- So if the dragged item is deactivated and re-activated during the drag (its subtree moved through a GlobalKey), it is no longer in `_items`.
- `_dragReset()` only resets `_items[_dragIndex]`:
  ```dart
  if (_dragIndex != null && _items.containsKey(_dragIndex)) { ... dragItem._dragging = false; ... }
  ```
- The re-activated item therefore keeps `_dragging == true` after `_dragInfo` is set to null, and every later `build` hits `_dragInfo!`.
- If the drop changes the order, the index-based `_ReorderableItemGlobalKey` replaces the item's state and the problem disappears. If the item is dropped in place, the stuck state survives.

A possible fix, not tested against the framework: re-register in `_ReorderableItemState.activate()`, and/or make `_dragReset` clear `_dragging` on every registered or known item instead of only `_items[_dragIndex]`.

The code is unchanged in 3.47.5, 3.48.0-0.5.pre, 3.49.0-0.1.pre and on `master` as of today.

### Code sample

<details open><summary>Code sample (runnable app)</summary>

```dart
import 'dart:async';

import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() => runApp(const MaterialApp(home: ReproPage()));

class ReproPage extends StatefulWidget {
  const ReproPage({super.key});

  @override
  State<ReproPage> createState() => _ReproPageState();
}

class _ReproPageState extends State<ReproPage> {
  final GlobalKey _listKey = GlobalKey();
  final List<String> _items = <String>['A', 'B', 'C', 'D'];
  late final Timer _timer;
  bool _wrapped = false;
  int _ticks = 0;

  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();
    // Rebuild once a second (like a stopwatch); every 3 seconds move the
    // list's subtree to a new parent through a GlobalKey.
    _timer = Timer.periodic(const Duration(seconds: 1), (_) {
      setState(() {
        _ticks++;
        if (_ticks % 3 == 0) {
          _wrapped = !_wrapped;
        }
      });
    });
  }

  @override
  void dispose() {
    _timer.cancel();
    super.dispose();
  }

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final Widget list = KeyedSubtree(
      key: _listKey,
      child: ReorderableListView.builder(
        itemCount: _items.length,
        onReorderItem: (int oldIndex, int newIndex) {
          setState(() => _items.insert(newIndex, _items.removeAt(oldIndex)));
        },
        itemBuilder: (BuildContext context, int index) => ListTile(
          key: ValueKey<String>(_items[index]),
          title: Text('Item ${_items[index]} · tick $_ticks'),
        ),
      ),
    );
    return Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(title: Text(_wrapped ? 'wrapped' : 'not wrapped')),
      body: _wrapped ? Padding(padding: EdgeInsets.zero, child: list) : list,
    );
  }
}
```

</details>

<details><summary>Deterministic widget test</summary>

```dart
import 'package:flutter/gestures.dart';
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';

class _Harness extends StatefulWidget {
  const _Harness({super.key});

  @override
  State<_Harness> createState() => _HarnessState();
}

class _HarnessState extends State<_Harness> {
  final GlobalKey _bodyKey = GlobalKey();
  final List<String> _ids = <String>['a', 'b', 'c'];
  bool _wrapped = false;
  int _generation = 0;

  void reparent() => setState(() => _wrapped = !_wrapped);
  void rebuild() => setState(() => _generation++);

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final Widget body = KeyedSubtree(
      key: _bodyKey,
      child: ReorderableListView.builder(
        itemCount: _ids.length,
        onReorderItem: (int oldIndex, int newIndex) {},
        itemBuilder: (BuildContext context, int index) => SizedBox(
          key: ValueKey<String>(_ids[index]),
          height: 80,
          child: Text('${_ids[index]} $_generation'),
        ),
      ),
    );
    return MaterialApp(
      home: Scaffold(
        body: _wrapped ? Padding(padding: EdgeInsets.zero, child: body) : body,
      ),
    );
  }
}

void main() {
  testWidgets('an item reparented mid-drag keeps dragging after the drop', (WidgetTester tester) async {
    final GlobalKey<_HarnessState> key = GlobalKey<_HarnessState>();
    await tester.pumpWidget(_Harness(key: key));

    final TestGesture drag = await tester.startGesture(tester.getCenter(find.text('b 0')));
    await tester.pump(kLongPressTimeout + const Duration(milliseconds: 50));
    await drag.moveBy(const Offset(0, 100));
    await tester.pump();

    key.currentState!.reparent(); // item "b" is deactivated + re-activated
    await tester.pump();

    await drag.moveBy(const Offset(0, -100)); // back where it started
    await tester.pump();
    await drag.up(); // throws once: Null check operator in _itemOffsetAt (_dragEnd)
    await tester.pump(const Duration(seconds: 1));

    key.currentState!.rebuild();
    await tester.pump(); // throws on every rebuild: Null check operator in _ReorderableItemState.build
  });
}
```

</details>

